 "notes": [
  "Document check: txt/2017-06-13_hermes_2017_rapportfinanciersemestriel_en.txt IS the H1 2017 half-year financial report (cover 'HALF-YEAR FINANCIAL REPORT JUNE 2017', statements at 30 June 2017, approved 13 Sep 2017); the 2017-06-13 date in the filename is wrong. H1/17 is taken from it; the H1 2017 results press release was used only for Q2/17 revenue.",
  "H1/12 is a comparative taken from the H1 2013 report (2013-08-29, IS p.16, revenue tables p.11, segment note p.26): only IS, sector revenue and geographic revenue. No constant-currency growth for H1/12 in that document. The H1/12 sector split includes Tableware 28.0 as a separate line.",
  "Sector reclassification: from the H1 2014 report (p.11), Tableware is no longer shown separately. La Table Hermès moves to 'Other Hermès sectors' and Saint-Louis/Puiforcat to 'Other products', applied retrospectively (restated H1/13: Other Hermès 109.7, Other products 98.6). H1/13 here keeps the original 2013 presentation (Other Hermès 94.7, Tableware 28.9, Other products 84.7).",
  "Free share plans reclassification (H1 2016 report, Note 7, p.28): from H1 2016 the free share plan expense (H1/16 21.1; H1/17 38.7) is in 'Other income and expenses' instead of SG&A. H1/15 was NOT restated on the face of the IS. Pro forma H1/15 is given in the note: OI&E 104.3 instead of 86.7, SG&A 676.3 instead of 693.9. Margins before and after 2016 are therefore not like-for-like in that split.",
  "Old cash-flow layout (all periods): there is no single 'Operating investments' line. Capex is split into 'Purchase of intangible assets' and 'Purchase of property, plant and equipment' (both in cf_other), so cf.capex = null. Use apm.operating_investments (key figures/Investments table) for capex. 'Investments in associates' / 'Acquisitions of subsidiaries and investments in associates' is mapped to cf.acq. 'Change in working capital' is mapped to d_wc, and cfo = 'Net cash from operating activities'. The FX on cash has three lines: fx = 'Effect of foreign currency exchange'; the 'scope of consolidation' and 'foreign currency exchange on intragroup transactions' lines are in cf_other and are included in the d_cash check. 'Impairment losses' is a separate CF add-back line next to D&A (in cf_other).",
  "bs: 'Investment property' is a separate non-current asset line every period (bs_other). Financial instruments in equity are mapped to reval_adj. equity_parent is not a line on the face of the balance sheet; it is taken from the statement of changes in equity / key figures ('Shareholders' equity', excluding NCI).",
  "memo.da_fixed = total D&A of PP&E and intangibles in operating expenses (cost of sales + OI&E), from the footnote to the 'Other income and expenses' note: 62.5 (H1/13), 68.3, 82.9, 92.0, 100.3 (H1/17). The OI&E-only depreciation line in that note is 52.9, 57.0, 69.5, 77.0, 82.8. memo.impairment = impairment losses line in the OI&E note, shown as a POSITIVE magnitude (printed negative): H1/15 3.8 is 'reversible impairment losses' (CF impairment add-back is 5.0, including goodwill), and H1/17 16.7 includes goodwill.",
  "memo.excep_tax: the 3% French tax on dividend distributions is included in the half-year estimated tax rate (expense, positive). H1/13 7.9 (2013 report Note 8.1, p.28); H1/14 8.4 (2014 report Note 9.1); H1/15 25 (2015 report Note 9.1, '3% tax on distribution of dividends for EUR 25 million', linked to the exceptional dividend). The H1 2016 report (Note 9.1) mentions EUR 17 million for the 3% tax on 2015 exceptional dividends to explain the rate variance vs 2015; it is not an H1/16 charge, so H1/16 is null. No company-published NI excluding these amounts.",
  "Exceptional dividend: an exceptional dividend of EUR 5.00 per share was PAID in H1 2015 (approved at AGM 2 June 2015, with the ordinary EUR 2.95 for FY2014; total EUR 830m; exceptional EUR 522m) (2015 report Note 21.1). CF dividends paid -840.4 includes NCI. Recorded as memo.dps_exceptional for H1/15.",
  "Interim dividends: EUR 1.50 interim paid 26 Feb 2016 (balance EUR 1.85 on 6 Jun 2016, FY2015 total EUR 3.35) and EUR 1.50 interim paid 24 Feb 2017 (balance EUR 2.25, FY2016 total EUR 3.75), so the H1 cash dividends include both parts.",
  "Segment ROI: the segment notes label it 'Operating income' / 'Operating results'. It equals ROI because non-recurring items are nil. 'Holding' column -> roi_unalloc. H1/17 segment total prints 931.2 vs IS ROI 931.3 (rounding; the column header is misprinted '01/06/2017').",
  "Non-recurring: 'Other non-recurring income and expense' is printed as nil (dash) in every period H1/12 to H1/17 (nonrec = 0).",
  "H1 2016 report prints EPS with comma decimals ('5,22', '5,20'), recorded as 5.22/5.20. Values printed '(0.0)' or '-' are recorded as 0.0.",
  "apm.restated_net_cash: no reconciliation is given in these H1 reports, so cash_inv_gt3m / fin_liab_restated are not available. bank_overdrafts are from the cash note ('Bank overdrafts and current accounts in debit'). Net cash = cash and cash equivalents less bank overdrafts (e.g. H1/17: 2442.3 - 8.1 = 2434.3). Gross borrowings are on the balance sheet.",
  "apm.operating_investments: 'Operating investments' from the Investments table (H1/13 74.3, H1/14 91.4, H1/15 100.4, H1/16 107.6, H1/17 104.8). Key figures 'Investments (excluding financial investments)' are 74.9, 130.3, 101.4, 107.6 and 105.2 (they also include investments in financial assets, e.g. H1/14 38.9 stake acquisitions).",
  "Q2 data: Q2/16 (1249.7, +8.1% cc, +6.2% reported) and Q2/17 (1361.3, +8.3% cc, +8.9% reported) are from the H1 results press releases (quarter tables). Q2/15 growth (+10% cc, +22% current) is rounded text from the H1 2015 report p.10. The H1 2015 release gives no Q2 figure. The 2016 release shows Q2 2015 revenue = 1,177.2 as a comparative (not recorded as Q2/15 revenue). Q2/14 +10% cc is rounded text from the H1 2014 report p.10. H1 2013 gives only Q2 retail +16.7% / wholesale +12.9% cc (no group figure), so there is no Q2/13.",
  "H1/13: the CF shows 'Cost of net debt' instead of the later 'Interest paid/received' lines. In H1/13 the cash note shows a large bank overdraft (192.3), so net cash 595.9 is below cash and cash equivalents of 787.5.",
  "H1/14 note: 'Acquisitions of subsidiaries and investments in associates' -38.9 (stake acquisitions, e.g. associates rose from 44.5 to 79.0). Treasury shares in equity improved to -266.7 from -313.9 because of free-share deliveries."
 ]
